---
description: Testing conventions for the NestJS + Nuxt monorepo.
globs: apps/**/test/**,apps/**/tests/**,apps/**/__tests__/**
alwaysApply: false
---

## Backend (NestJS)

- Use Jest (`apps/api` scripts).
- Prefer unit tests for services and utilities.
- Use `@nestjs/testing` to build testing modules when needed.
- Mock external dependencies at module boundaries.
- Avoid integration tests unless they add clear value.

## Frontend (Nuxt)

- Follow any existing test runner configuration in `apps/pwa`.
- If no frontend test setup exists, avoid introducing one unless explicitly requested.
